  "stem": "\\[2x + 3y = 16\\] \\[3x - y = 2\\] If \\((x, y)\\) is the solution to the system of equations above, what is the value of \\(xy\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "8"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "From the second equation, \\(y = 3x - 2\\).",
    "Substitute: \\(2x + 3(3x - 2) = 16\\), so \\(11x - 6 = 16\\) and \\(x = 2\\).",
    "Then \\(y = 3(2) - 2 = 4\\), so \\(xy = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x, y = symbols('x y')\nsol = solve([2*x + 3*y - 16, 3*x - y - 2], [x, y])\nassert sol == {x: 2, y: 4}\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == [sol[x]*sol[y]]",
